Slice A of the Beads-removal epic (9502879b; folds 454deef3). Consolidate to a
single kernel-sourced dashboard: 'forge status' (CLI) + 'forge serve' (browser).
- DELETE lib/commands/board.js — it read readBeadsSnapshot (.beads/issues.jsonl,
  a legacy file) while falsely describing itself 'from kernel state'.
- DELETE scripts/forge-team/lib/dashboard.sh + its wiring/tests (the duplicate
  bash team-dashboard render) + drop it from setup.js WORKFLOW_RUNTIME_ASSETS.
- lib/status/presenter.js: reword 'local Beads runtime state' -> 'kernel state';
  remove now-dead formatBoard/buildBoardJson (only board.js used them).
- skills/coverage.json: drop the board entry (command removed).
Survivors verified: 'forge status' renders; 'forge board' -> unknown command.
lint clean; status-command 34/0 (15s lane timeout); coverage gate 0 gaps.
serve->dash rename + 'status --text' are the immediate next PR (separate concern).

Plan: docs/work/2026-07-22-beads-removal/plan.md. Closes bcb5115c.

